<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Dutch Wars</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Dutch Wars</a> were a series of naval wars fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries. They arose from commercial and maritime rivalry over trade and shipping. The conflicts tested the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>'s naval power and contributed to the gradual shift of commercial supremacy towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-dutch-wars.jpg" alt="Anglo-Dutch Wars" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abraham Storck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Storck,_Four_Days_Battle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
